course: dictionary
lesson: 3879
title: Big words with more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. The word freedom means being free, a particular right, or not having something bad. «Freedom of religion means everyone may believe what they choose.» Here freedom is a right that people have.
explain: The first meaning is about being free: able to go where you like, say what you think and choose what to do. «Many peasants won more freedom» tells you that people gained more control over their own lives.
explain: Look for clues in the words around the word. «Freedom from fear» means not having fear. «Freedom ends where it hurts someone else» reminds you that freedom comes with responsibilities. Always try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Freedom means being free: able to go where you like, say what you think and choose what to do.
fact: A freedom is a particular right, such as freedom of speech or freedom of religion.
fact: Freedom from something means not having it, as in «freedom from fear».
fact: In history, freedom is won by ending slavery and unfair laws. In the Bible story of Exodus, God leads the Israelites from slavery to freedom.
fact: Freedoms come with responsibilities: your freedom ends where it hurts someone else.
exercise: «Enslaved people worked without pay or freedom.» What does freedom mean in this sentence? | Having lots of money to spend | *Being free to go where you like and choose what to do | Learning to read and write | Being paid for every hour of work
exercise: «Freedom from fear» means what? | Running away quickly from danger | Having a fear of heights | Being very frightened all the time | *Not having fear
exercise: Freedom of speech is one of the freedoms people fight for. What is a freedom in this sentence? | A rule that stops you talking in class | A type of bird that cannot fly | A big open field with no fences | *A particular right, like freedom of speech
test: «Rights are things every person is entitled to, such as safety, education, being heard and freedom of belief.» Which of these is named as a right? | Long holidays with no homework | Sleeping in until noon | *Education | Ice cream every day
test: In a story, a caged bird flying away shows which idea? | Anger | *Freedom | Hunger | Sleep
exam: «Freedoms come with responsibilities: your freedom ends where it hurts someone else.» What does this mean? | You can do anything you like, always | Freedom means there are never any rules | *Your freedom must not harm other people | Freedom only applies to adults
